  "answer": "<p>The correct configuration is <b>Cloud Pub/Sub with a quota of 162,000 messages per second and 10 MB average message size</b>.</p><p>This matches the projected growth. The current peak of 90,000 messages per second increased by 80 percent becomes 162,000 messages per second, and the average message size of 8 MB increased by 25 percent becomes 10 MB. Right sizing to the forecasted peak meets the requirement while controlling costs. Cloud Pub/Sub provides high durability across zones, so the durability requirement is satisfied with this choice.</p><p>Multiplying 90,000 by 1.8 gives 162,000 messages per second, and multiplying 8 MB by 1.25 gives 10 MB. Choosing a quota that aligns with the projected peak avoids unnecessary overprovisioning and reduces the risk of throttling during bursts.</p><p><i>Cloud Pub/Sub with a quota of 250,000 messages per second and 12 MB average message size</i> significantly overprovisions both rate and size compared to the forecast, which can lead to unnecessary cost without improving the outcome.</p><p><i>Cloud Pub/Sub with a quota of 162,000 messages per second and 8 MB average message size</i> keeps the correct message rate but underestimates the post growth message size, which risks backlog growth and throughput pressure at peak.</p><p><i>Cloud Pub/Sub with a quota of 320,000 messages per second and 15 MB average message size</i> greatly exceeds the projected needs on both dimensions, which is unnecessary and does not help control costs.</p>",
